{"id":"word:hebrew:H7402","type":"word","title":"רָכַל","subtitle":"H7402 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to travel for trading","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to רָכַל (H7402) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 17 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"רָכַל (râkal) means to travel for trading First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 10 15."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"רָכַל","transliteration":"râkal","pronunciation":"raw-kal'","strong":"H7402","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7402","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["רֹֽכְלַ֔יִ/ךְ","רֹכְלָ֑יִ/ךְ","הָ/רֹכְלִ֑ים","רֹכְלִ֖ים","רֹכֶ֨לֶת֙"],"morphs":[["HVqrmpc/Sp2fs",6],["HTd/Vqrmpa",2],["HVqrfsc/Sp2fs",2],["HVqrmpc",2],["HC/Td/Vqrmpa",2],["HVqrmpa",1],["HVqrfsc",1],["HVqrmsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to travel for trading","usage":"(spice) merchant.","full":"H7402. rakal [ רָכַל ] verb probably go about, from one to another (for trade or gossip) (? connected with רגל ; compare Arabic kick a horse, to make him go [? properly use the foot , compare ?]; Late Hebrew רוֺכֵל , Aramaic רוֺכְלָא , trader , Late Hebrew רְכִילוּת slander [compare calumniator , from go about , Qor 2:19 and elsewhere]); — Qal Participle רוֺכֵל Song 3:6 ; feminine singular construct רֹכֶ֫לֶת Ezek 27:3 , suffix רֹכַלְתֵךְ 27:20 ; 27:23 ; masculine plural רֹכְלִים 1Kin 10:15 +, etc.; — as substantive = trafficker, trader: usually plural, Nahum 3:16 ; Ezek 17:4 ( ר ׳עִיר ), 27:13 , 15 , 17 , 22 (twice in verse); 27:23 a (&lt; strike out Toy Krae), 27:24 ; Neh 3:31-32 , 13:20 ( + כָלמִֿמְכָּר מֹרֵי ); הָר ׳מִסְחַר 1Kin 10:15 (text dubious; compare ׳מ p.695); singular figurative of Tyre, רַכִּים אֶלאִֿיִּים הָעַמִּים רֹכֶלֶת Ezek 27:8 , of a people 27:20 ; 27:23 b (plural Mez Harran 34 Krae, see also כִּלְמֶד ); singular of person only רוֺכֵל אַבְקַת Song 3:6 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurren